---
import Layout from "../layouts/Layout.astro";
import PageHero from "../components/PageHero.astro";
import DataLayers from "../components/DataLayers.astro";
import DeployTable from "../components/DeployTable.astro";
import { href, ext } from "../lib/site";

const tiers = [
  { name: "Hosted", tag: "managed · Swiss/EU data residency",
    body: "Your data rests on Swiss/EU infrastructure; that is the residency promise. The service around it runs with providers in Switzerland and the USA, named on our privacy page. Nothing to maintain on your side: connect your system of record and go.",
    gist: "nothing to maintain on your side" },
  { name: "Hybrid", tag: "on-site data · structured results sync",
    body: "Raw documents and delicate data never leave your premises: a small on-site device runs the host and storage. Extracted, structured results sync to Swiss/EU infrastructure.",
    gist: "raw documents stay on your premises" },
  { name: "On-premises", tag: "your hardware · your control",
    body: "The full stack on infrastructure you control, for organisations or schools that require complete data and compute sovereignty. The source is yours under AGPL-3.0.",
    gist: "complete data and compute sovereignty" },
];
---
<Layout title="Back-office tooling for accounting and HR" description="Back-office tooling for accounting, HR and consulting in Swiss organisations. Every step leaves a sealed audit record. CashCtrl first, more via the open API.">
  <PageHero
    eyebrow="Back office"
    title="Accounting, contracts and the recurring tasks around them."
    lede="Purpose-built tools that call the APIs of the platforms you already use. Responsibility stays with the human operator. In development alongside the engine.">
    <div class="actions">
      <a class="btn" href={href("/request-access/?interest=accounting")}>Start with a pilot</a>
      <a class="link" href="#deploy">Where it runs</a>
    </div>
  </PageHero>

  <!-- What we offer -->
  <section class="section">
    <div class="wrap">
      <p class="eyebrow">What we offer</p>
      <h2 class="h2">Tools, and the thinking around them.</h2>
      <div class="grid grid--2" data-shape="offer">
        <article class="card">
          <div class="card__head"><h3>Tools</h3><span class="chip">first server public</span></div>
          <p class="for">for the systems a school already runs</p>
          <p>Model Context Protocol servers that let an assistant work against the systems already in use rather than replacing them. The scope is accounting, contracting and data gathering. Each server exposes a fixed vocabulary of permitted operations, so what it is able to do can be read before it does anything.</p>
          <a class="link" href={ext.lp21}>Lehrplan 21 MCP: read the source</a>
        </article>
        <article class="card">
          <div class="card__head"><h3>Consulting</h3><span class="chip">on request</span></div>
          <p class="for">for the whole working perspective, not one tool</p>
          <p>entrosana’s way of working applied to your situation: what is worth automating, what stays with your people, and what the record has to capture for either to be checkable. Delivered with the decision path, so a recommendation can be traced rather than taken on trust.</p>
          <a class="link" href={href("/request-access/?interest=consulting")}>Ask for consulting</a>
        </article>
      </div>
      <p class="xref small">Looking for learning modules for a class? <a href={href("/modules/")}>They have their own page</a>.</p>
    </div>
  </section>

  <!-- Data boundary -->
  <section class="section" id="data">
    <div class="wrap">
      <p class="eyebrow">How data is handled</p>
      <h2 class="h2">Two model layers, by design.</h2>
      <p class="intro">Calls that touch sensitive records are designed to run on a locally served model; the rest may go to an online one. That division is what keeps data management local rather than merely promised.</p>
      <DataLayers />
    </div>
  </section>

  <!-- Connectors -->
  <section class="section band">
    <div class="wrap split">
      <div>
        <p class="eyebrow">Connectors</p>
        <h2 class="h2">The choice of provider stays yours.</h2>
      </div>
      <div>
        <p>The code is adaptive: the design includes a neutral API connector that can be adjusted to your environment, whether you run CashCtrl, bexio or another platform. Connectors are verified offline so far, not yet against a live provider account; the <a href={href("/roadmap/")}>roadmap</a> says what that still needs.</p>
        <p>Open to contributors: connectors and workflow adapters built by API engineers with an educative approach are welcome.</p>
        <div class="actions">
          <a class="btn btn--ghost" href={ext.source}>Contribute a connector</a>
        </div>
      </div>
    </div>
  </section>

  <!-- Where it runs -->
  <section class="section" id="deploy">
    <div class="wrap">
      <p class="eyebrow">Where it runs</p>
      <h2 class="h2">You bring the demand. We provide the base.</h2>
      <p class="intro">Three ways to run it, all in development. For an organisation answerable to the Swiss Data Protection Act (revDSG) or to the GDPR, this choice is the data protection decision: where the data sits, who can reach it, and what record exists of every step.</p>
      <DeployTable />
      <div class="grid grid--3 tiers" data-shape="spectrum">
        {tiers.map((t) => (
          <article class="card">
            <p class="tag">{t.tag}</p>
            <h3>{t.name}</h3>
            <span class="chip chip--dev">in development</span>
            <p>{t.body}</p>
            <p class="for">→ {t.gist}</p>
          </article>
        ))}
      </div>
      <p class="xref small">What each tier still needs is on the <a href={href("/roadmap/#tiers")}>roadmap</a>. What this site itself processes is on the <a href={href("/privacy/")}>privacy page</a>.</p>
    </div>
  </section>

  <!-- Pilot -->
  <section class="section band">
    <div class="wrap split split--stack">
      <div>
        <p class="eyebrow">Get started</p>
        <h2 class="h2">Start with a pilot.</h2>
      </div>
      <div>
        <p>Pilots are temporary projects and can become permanent if they prove useful. Pilot pricing is reduced, and we are glad to work alongside foundations interested in innovative education and technology.</p>
        <p class="small muted">On our legal form: entrosana intends to become a non-profit organisation once its financial base is established.</p>
        <div class="actions">
          <a class="btn" href={href("/request-access/?interest=accounting")}>Request pilot access</a>
          <a class="link" href={ext.source}>View the source</a>
        </div>
      </div>
    </div>
  </section>
</Layout>

<style is:global>
.section .tiers { margin-top: 2.4rem; }                              /* live: below the figure */
.xref { margin-top: 1.25rem; color: var(--muted); }

</style>
